<%# HOME'S COLUMN (Shop manual spec §7): the page's own sections as in-page links, then Pinned — the
    pinned folders and pinned tools the rail used to carry on every page. Home lights no place and no
    row (spec §11.2): a section link is a place on this page, not a page.

    THE SECTIONS ARE THE ONES HomeController#index RENDERS, NUMBERED AS THE PAGE NUMBERS THEM:
    HomeHelper#home_sections is the one list both read (Shop manual slice 7), and it is empty on any
    other Home page (the onboarding wizard is Home's too and shows none of them). A row carries its
    section's count where it has one. shell_layout_test.rb holds every in-page link to an element the
    page carries, so a section that leaves the page cannot leave its link behind.

    THE PINNED TOOLS keep their right-click Unpin (`toolmenu`) and the calculator keeps its opener: a
    real href all the same, so a modified click, or a page whose script failed, lands on the Tools
    card that opens it. %>
<% sections = home_sections %>
<% tools = current_user.tool_pins.to_a %>
<% if sections.any? %>
  <div class="column-group">
    <h2 class="column-head">On this page</h2>
    <% sections.each do |section| %>
      <%= column_row safe_join([ tag.span(section.number, class: "column-row-num"), " ", section.label ]),
                     "##{section.id}", note: section.count %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
<% if sidebar_pins.any? || tools.any? %>
  <div class="column-group" data-controller="toolmenu">
    <h2 class="column-head">Pinned</h2>
    <% sidebar_pins.each do |pin, name| %>
      <%= column_row name, files_path(folder: pin.node_id), note: "folder" %>
    <% end %>
    <%= render "layouts/column/tool_pins", tools: tools %>
  </div>
<% end %>
